(7421178, 1170735, 49109, '<td valign="top">For me that''s not an artistic but a product shot (being a product photographer myself). As that, the lack of focus/DOF is detrimental. I also found the crop to be too loose and the dust/lint distracting (didn''t vote, but would have given an 5).</td>', 'For me that''s not an artistic but a product shot (being a product photographer myself). As that, the lack of focus/DOF is detrimental. I also found the crop to be too loose and the dust/lint distracting (didn''t vote, but would have given an 5).', '2015-12-08 10:29:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(7421180, 1170084, 113411, '<td valign="top">Too fabulous, Dennis.  Congratulations!</td>', 'Too fabulous, Dennis.  Congratulations!', '2015-12-08 10:36:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(7421181, 1170478, 35804, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the Blue. You''ve made drops cool again! Now try to make one that looks like a bear jumping through a fiery hoop...I dare you...or maybe a seal balancing a colorful ball on it''s nose?</td>', 'Congrats on the Blue. You''ve made drops cool again! Now try to make one that looks like a bear jumping through a fiery hoop...I dare you...or maybe a seal balancing a colorful ball on it''s nose?', '2015-12-08 10:38:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(7421183, 1171149, 113411, '<td valign="top">Fabulous shot, fabulous dog! Congratulations Mary Ann!</td>', 'Fabulous shot, fabulous dog! Congratulations Mary Ann!', '2015-12-08 10:41:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(7421184, 1171028, 86447, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>This is really lovely, Janine!   <br/> <br/>Those trees and the road leading us in from everywhere are effective and gorgeous.   The colors seem a bit off... the purple ground, but the greens are fabulous.  <br/> <br/>I gave it a 7 during voting.   I do get just a bit disappointed when I get to where all of those leading lines led me and... there''s just brightness.  I find myself wanting an ''exclamation point'' there instead of a ''period''.   Perhaps two people holding hands silhouetted? Maybe not even a dark silhouette... just a suggestion of a person/people.<br/> <br/>I dunno... but I probably would have given an 8 or 9 with a surprise at the end after such a gorgeous build-up.<br/> <br/>Still, it''s a fabulously lovely image, Janine.  You should be proud of it.<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! This is really lovely, Janine!    Those trees and the road leading us in from everywhere are effective and gorgeous.   The colors seem a bit off... the purple ground, but the greens are fabulous.   I gave it a 7 during voting.   I do get just a bit disappointed when I get to where all of those leading lines led me and... there''s just brightness.  I find myself wanting an ''exclamation point'' there instead of a ''period''.   Perhaps two people holding hands silhouetted? Maybe not even a dark silhouette... just a suggestion of a person/people. I dunno... but I probably would have given an 8 or 9 with a surprise at the end after such a gorgeous build-up. Still, it''s a fabulously lovely image, Janine.  You should be proud of it.', '2015-12-08 10:41:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7421185, 1171022, 113411, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Mark! Wonderful shot.</td>', 'Congratulations Mark! Wonderful shot.', '2015-12-08 10:42:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(7421187, 1170735, 35804, '<td valign="top">I gave it a 4...I would have liked it more without the ring, and as Oliver mentioned the dust/pollen could have been cloned or healed out. To my eye, the comp is off. Had the ring been gone and the image rotated 90 degrees clockwise or counter clockwise, I probably would have given a much higher score...the colors are quite lovely.</td>', 'I gave it a 4...I would have liked it more without the ring, and as Oliver mentioned the dust/pollen could have been cloned or healed out. To my eye, the comp is off. Had the ring been gone and the image rotated 90 degrees clockwise or counter clockwise, I probably would have given a much higher score...the colors are quite lovely.', '2015-12-08 10:46:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(7421188, 1170735, 2764, '<td valign="top">The yellow looks like an eye and the white on the right looks like teeth making it kind of creepy.  I like the ring on the purple but there is too much competing with it.</td>', 'The yellow looks like an eye and the white on the right looks like teeth making it kind of creepy.  I like the ring on the purple but there is too much competing with it.', '2015-12-08 10:57:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7421196, 1171113, 78191, '<td valign="top">Verrazano Bridge</td>', 'Verrazano Bridge', '2015-12-08 12:23:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(7421197, 1170735, 43565, '<td valign="top">I gave it a 4. The ring (which I took to be the subject) is not in focus and is too centered for me. Also, to me the most interesting part of the iris is where the yellow meets the purple, and that is not in focus either.</td>', 'I gave it a 4. The ring (which I took to be the subject) is not in focus and is too centered for me. Also, to me the most interesting part of the iris is where the yellow meets the purple, and that is not in focus either.', '2015-12-08 12:24:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7421199, 1170735, 38032, '<td valign="top">Jewelry in NOT easy to photograph well. It is small, reflective, and somewhat unforgiving. So your subject is tough to start IMHO.<br/>The background and ring are equally banal when combined here. Neither is being explored and they don''t relate to each other in a cohesive way. A more interesting composition or more detailed macro would add some interest. I gave it a 5 for the good lighting and color.</td>', 'Jewelry in NOT easy to photograph well. It is small, reflective, and somewhat unforgiving. So your subject is tough to start IMHO.The background and ring are equally banal when combined here. Neither is being explored and they don''t relate to each other in a cohesive way. A more interesting composition or more detailed macro would add some interest. I gave it a 5 for the good lighting and color.', '2015-12-08 12:39:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(7421200, 1170735, 72268, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by h2:</b></div><hr/><i> For me that''s not an artistic but a product shot (being a product photographer myself). As that, the lack of focus/DOF is detrimental. I also found the crop to be too loose and the dust/lint distracting (didn''t vote, but would have given an 5). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes it is a product but whos not to say that a product shot can''t be artistic? I do appreciate your comment though. I do agree with the ring not being in sharp focus as I previously stated, however the rest of the photograph is very interesting, and I don''t think cropping it tighter would have made this photograph better, and in fact would have taken away from it.<br/>Thanks again for your comment.</td>', 'Originally posted by h2: For me that''s not an artistic but a product shot (being a product photographer myself). As that, the lack of focus/DOF is detrimental. I also found the crop to be too loose and the dust/lint distracting (didn''t vote, but would have given an 5).   Yes it is a product but whos not to say that a product shot can''t be artistic? I do appreciate your comment though. I do agree with the ring not being in sharp focus as I previously stated, however the rest of the photograph is very interesting, and I don''t think cropping it tighter would have made this photograph better, and in fact would have taken away from it.Thanks again for your comment.', '2015-12-08 12:43:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(7421201, 1170735, 72268, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Elaine:</b></div><hr/><i> I gave it a 4. The ring (which I took to be the subject) is not in focus and is too centered for me. Also, to me the most interesting part of the iris is where the yellow meets the purple, and that is not in focus either. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you for your comment! The part you found the most interesting was supposed to be blurred lol</td>', 'Originally posted by Elaine: I gave it a 4. The ring (which I took to be the subject) is not in focus and is too centered for me. Also, to me the most interesting part of the iris is where the yellow meets the purple, and that is not in focus either.   Thank you for your comment! The part you found the most interesting was supposed to be blurred lol', '2015-12-08 12:45:25.000000', NULL, 0),
